WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.535
Deep work and outreach need protected blocks.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.346
Hope is not a schedule.

00:00:04.346 --> 00:00:07.243
This lesson is about calendar blocks that stick.

00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:09.053
Protect deep work and outreach.

00:00:09.053 --> 00:00:11.588
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.588 --> 00:00:15.209
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:20.641
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:24.625
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:28.608
Stay practical: block next week before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:33.102
Block next week on a real calendar: delivery, outreach, and learning.

00:00:33.102 --> 00:00:35.379
Remember the objective: block next week.

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:39.553
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:44.106
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:48.280
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.834
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.490
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.008
Feedback beats guessing alone.

